<title>GERMANY: Koebnick-Timing of Buba act changes unfortunate.</title>
<headline>Koebnick-Timing of Buba act changes unfortunate.</headline>
<dateline>MAINZ, Germany 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Hans-Juergen Koebnick said on Wednesday that the timing of the announcement last Thursday of plans to revalue the Bundesbank reserves of currency and gold was unfortunate.</p>
<p>Koebnick said the announcement coincided with the official tax revenue estimate for 1997 and with a debate about Germany's efforts to qualify for monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;It was not a happy coincidence that it was announced in this period and I think that lawmakers must look carefully at the federal republic's and the Bundesbank's position in the process towards EMU,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Koebnick said he did not want to give a comment on the finance ministry's plan itself before the ministry had presented draft proposals to the Bundesbank.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
